# FragranceDNA Environment Variables

## Persistent User Database (Neon PostgreSQL)
# Create a Neon project from Vercel Marketplace and copy its pooled connection string.
# Add these values to .env.local for development and Vercel Environment Variables for production.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/DATABASE?sslmode=require

# Generate a unique random secret (at least 32 bytes). Keep private and identical across Vercel environments.
AUTH_SESSION_SECRET=replace_with_a_long_random_secret

# Seed the FragranceDNA Studio administrator on first Neon access. Use a dedicated strong password.
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
ADMIN_PASSWORD=replace_with_a_strong_unique_password

## Authentication Configuration

### Email/Password Authentication
# Email/password accounts and user profiles use Neon when DATABASE_URL is configured.
# The browser only keeps a cache; server-authenticated sessions use an HttpOnly cookie.

### Google OAuth 2.0 Configuration
# Get these from Google Cloud Console: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# The "Continue with Google" button only appears when NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID is set.

# OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application)
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_client_id_here

# OAuth 2.0 Client Secret (keep this private, use in .env.local only)
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_google_client_secret_here

# Optional: override the redirect URI. Defaults to {origin}/api/auth/oauth/google/callback
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/auth/oauth/google/callback

### Apple Sign In Configuration
# Requires a paid Apple Developer account: https://developer.apple.com/
# The "Continue with Apple" button only appears when NEXT_PUBLIC_APPLE_SERVICE_ID is set.

# Apple Service ID (Bundle ID format)
NEXT_PUBLIC_APPLE_SERVICE_ID=com.fragrance-dna.web

# Apple Team ID
APPLE_TEAM_ID=your_apple_team_id

# Apple Key ID
APPLE_KEY_ID=your_apple_key_id

# Apple Private Key (PEM contents; newlines may be escaped as \n)
APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY=your_apple_private_key_here

# Optional: override the redirect URI. Defaults to {origin}/api/auth/oauth/apple/callback
# APPLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=https://olfactivedna.com/api/auth/oauth/apple/callback

## Production Deployment

# Vercel Environment
NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_URL=https://olfactivedna.com

# Update OAuth redirect URIs for production (Google Console / Apple Developer):
# https://olfactivedna.com/api/auth/oauth/google/callback
# https://olfactivedna.com/api/auth/oauth/apple/callback

## Development Notes

### Google CSE Enrichment (optional)
# Used by scripts/enrich-perfumes-from-google-cse.mjs to fill missing fields.
GOOGLE_CSE_API_KEY=your_google_custom_search_api_key
GOOGLE_CSE_CX=your_google_custom_search_engine_id
# Optional limits for batch execution safety
GOOGLE_ENRICH_LIMIT=200
GOOGLE_ENRICH_DELAY_MS=150

### AI-generated local perfume images (optional)
# Required only when running `npm run images:generate`.
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key
# Optional. Defaults to gpt-image-1.
OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-1

### Product photos in Vercel Blob
# Server/script-only credential, provisioned by the connected public Blob store.
# Never use NEXT_PUBLIC_ for this token.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=your_vercel_blob_read_write_token

### Setting Up Google OAuth:
1. Create a Google Cloud project and open APIs & Services → Credentials
2. Configure the OAuth consent screen (External, add your app name and domain)
3. Create OAuth 2.0 credentials (Web Application)
4. Add authorized redirect URIs:
   - http://localhost:3000/api/auth/oauth/google/callback
   - https://olfactivedna.com/api/auth/oauth/google/callback
5. Copy Client ID to NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
6. Copy Client Secret to GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET

### Setting Up Apple Sign In:
1. Enroll in the Apple Developer Program (paid)
2. Register an App ID with the "Sign In with Apple" capability
3. Create a Services ID, enable Sign In with Apple, register the production domain
   and the https://olfactivedna.com/api/auth/oauth/apple/callback return URL
4. Generate a Sign In with Apple private key (note the Key ID)
5. Copy values to NEXT_PUBLIC_APPLE_SERVICE_ID, APPLE_TEAM_ID, APPLE_KEY_ID, APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY

### Local Development:
- Copy this file to .env.local
- Replace placeholders with actual values
- Never commit .env.local to version control
# Use email/password authentication during development if real OAuth credentials are not configured.

### Testing Authentication:
- Email sign-in: real accounts stored in Neon (or data/generated/auth-users.json when DATABASE_URL is unset)
- Google OAuth: real authorization code flow; works on localhost once Google credentials are set
- Apple OAuth: real flow; requires HTTPS, so it can only be tested on the deployed domain
- Session: HttpOnly signed cookie; localStorage is only a display cache
